WEBVTT

00:00:10.957 --> 00:00:13.078
Lucky Number by John Milne.

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:18.490
Café Colombo is always busy.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:23.592
There are always people sitting at the tables in Café Colombo.

00:00:23.652 --> 00:00:27.343
The men and women are all well-dressed.

00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:29.494
They drink coffee.

00:00:29.554 --> 00:00:31.524
They eat ice-cream.

00:00:31.585 --> 00:00:33.425
They read newspapers.

00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:38.788
Charlie does not sit in Café Colombo.

00:00:38.848 --> 00:00:42.011
Charlie is not well-dressed.

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:46.643
He sits on the pavement outside Café Colombo.

00:00:46.703 --> 00:00:49.114
He sits on a small box.

00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:53.656
Charlie is a shoeshine boy.

00:00:53.716 --> 00:00:56.427
Charlie shines shoes.

00:00:56.487 --> 00:00:58.848
He does not go to school.

00:00:58.908 --> 00:01:01.139
He works all day.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.539
Charlie shines men's shoes.

00:01:09.599 --> 00:01:12.576
He shines ladies' shoes.

00:01:12.636 --> 00:01:15.367
He shines black shoes.

00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:18.228
He shines brown shoes.

00:01:18.288 --> 00:01:21.638
He shines blue shoes.

00:01:21.698 --> 00:01:25.249
"Shoeshine! Shoeshine!"

00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:30.520
"Ten cents! Ten cents! Ten cents a shine!"

00:01:36.281 --> 00:01:38.872
A man in Café Colombo shouts.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.384
"Charlie!"

00:01:40.444 --> 00:01:43.747
Charlie runs into Café Colombo.

00:01:43.807 --> 00:01:46.789
He puts his box at the man's feet.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:50.312
The man puts one foot on the box.

00:01:50.372 --> 00:01:53.624
The man's shoes are black.

00:01:53.684 --> 00:01:56.886
The man's shoes are dirty.

00:01:56.946 --> 00:01:59.698
Charlie cleans the man's shoes.

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:04.742
The man gives Charlie ten cents.

00:02:04.802 --> 00:02:08.004
Charlie takes the ten-cent coin.

00:02:08.064 --> 00:02:10.423
He picks up his box.

00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:12.822
He goes back to the pavement.

00:02:18.644 --> 00:02:22.076
An old man walks slowly along the pavement.

00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:26.098
The old man is carrying a large board.

00:02:26.158 --> 00:02:29.068
There is a notice on the board.

00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:33.211
The old man is selling lottery tickets.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.522
"Buy a ticket!"

00:02:35.582 --> 00:02:37.392
"Win a fortune!"

00:02:37.452 --> 00:02:39.759
"One dollar a ticket!"

00:02:39.819 --> 00:02:43.066
"Give me a ticket! Hurry!"

00:02:43.126 --> 00:02:48.008
A well-dressed man in Café Colombo is shouting.

00:02:48.068 --> 00:02:51.820
The ticket-seller gives the man a ticket.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.812
The man gives the ticket-seller a dollar.

00:02:59.034 --> 00:03:01.476
The well-dressed man is in a hurry.

00:03:01.535 --> 00:03:03.626
A taxi is waiting.

00:03:03.686 --> 00:03:07.508
The man puts the ticket in his pocket quickly.

00:03:07.568 --> 00:03:10.549
The man gets into the taxi.

00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:13.730
The ticket falls out of his pocket.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.822
The wind blows the ticket into the air.

00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:20.803
Charlie catches the ticket.

00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:24.234
He has the ticket in his hand.

00:03:24.294 --> 00:03:27.257
Charlie waves his arms.

00:03:27.316 --> 00:03:29.498
He shouts out loudly.

00:03:29.558 --> 00:03:32.740
"Your ticket! Your ticket!"

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.671
The man does not hear Charlie.

00:03:35.731 --> 00:03:38.366
The taxi moves away.

00:03:38.426 --> 00:03:41.311
Charlie stands on the pavement.

00:03:41.371 --> 00:03:43.681
The ticket is in his hand.

00:03:50.103 --> 00:03:52.874
Café Colombo closes at midnight.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:56.285
Charlie's home is far away.

00:03:56.345 --> 00:04:00.686
Every night, Charlie has a long walk home.

00:04:02.907 --> 00:04:05.268
Charlie's mother is waiting for him.

00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:07.208
He gives her all the money.

00:04:09.335 --> 00:04:11.746
Charlie has no father.

00:04:11.806 --> 00:04:16.048
Charlie has younger brothers and younger sisters.

00:04:16.108 --> 00:04:19.658
Charlie's mother needs the money.

00:04:19.718 --> 00:04:22.219
She buys food with the money.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:27.461
Charlie shows his mother the lottery ticket.

00:04:27.521 --> 00:04:30.463
His mother looks at the ticket.

00:04:30.522 --> 00:04:33.274
She reads the number.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:49.900
"Seven, five, three, eight, one, two, nine, four, six."

00:04:50.016 --> 00:04:52.558
Is this the winning number?

00:04:52.617 --> 00:04:55.039
Perhaps it is.

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:59.182
Saturday the 21st is tomorrow.

00:04:59.242 --> 00:05:03.584
Perhaps tomorrow will be their lucky day.

00:05:08.633 --> 00:05:10.494
Charlie is tired.

00:05:10.554 --> 00:05:13.696
He puts the ticket on his box.

00:05:13.756 --> 00:05:15.917
He falls asleep.

00:05:18.179 --> 00:05:20.600
Charlie has a dream.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.884
A goat comes into the house.

00:05:25.944 --> 00:05:29.446
The goat finds the ticket.

00:05:29.506 --> 00:05:33.458
The goat is eating the ticket.

00:05:33.518 --> 00:05:38.105
The goat eats the number six.

00:05:38.164 --> 00:05:42.132
The goat eats the number four.

00:05:42.192 --> 00:05:45.725
The goat eats the number nine.

00:05:49.068 --> 00:05:50.760
Charlie wakes up.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.932
It is morning.

00:05:52.992 --> 00:05:56.434
The ticket is not on the box.

00:05:56.494 --> 00:05:58.716
Where is the ticket?

00:06:00.798 --> 00:06:03.691
Charlie runs to the lottery office.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.596
Charlie sees his mother.

00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:09.449
She has the ticket.

00:06:11.529 --> 00:06:15.190
A man is shouting out the winning number.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:28.324
"Seven, five, three, eight, one, two, nine, four."

00:06:28.384 --> 00:06:32.806
Will the next number be six?

00:06:32.866 --> 00:06:36.647
Will it be their lucky number?

00:06:36.707 --> 00:06:54.000
Will it be their lucky day?